<title>USA: St Louis feeder cattle steady-off $3 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Louis feeder cattle steady-off $3 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>EAST ST LOUIS, Ill. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>FEEDER CATTLE AUCTION:  325 head. Compared with last week, feeder steers and heifers under 400 lbs and over 600 lbs. generally steady. 400 to 600 lbs. of both classes fully $2.00-$3.00 per cwt lower.</p>
<p>Overall quality below last weeks level.Large buyer attendance.</p>
<p>FEEDER STEERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>Thin:     300-400 lbs. 83.00-88.00, package 275 lbs.</p>
<p>Crossbreds at 91.25</p>
<p>400-500 lbs. 79.00-86.00</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 76.00-82.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 74.00-79.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 70.00-75.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:  400-600 lbs. 72.00-79.00</p>
<p>LARGE FRAME 2 HOLSTEINS: 300-700 lbs. 59.00-62.00</p>
<p>FEEDER HEIFERS:  Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>Thin:     300-400 lbs. 73.00-80.00</p>
<p>400-500 lbs. 72.00-78.00</p>
<p>Several  500-600 lbs. 71.00-76.00, Crossbreds 76.00-78.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 69.00-73.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:</p>
<p>400-600 lbs. 67.00-73.00</p>
<p>Receipts 325  Last week  350  Last Year 300</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
